cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research project, please cite the author and manuscript."
title: "Lubuimi's Terminal-Residue Collision Energy"
authors:
  - family-names: Lubuimi
    given-names: Ta-Yoshua
date-released: 2026-11-10
version: "0.1.0"
type: article
abstract: >-
  A finite-place second-moment identity for accelerated-Syracuse valuation
  words. The manuscript proves an exact diagonal/off-diagonal decomposition,
  a forced lower bound for terminal-residue collision mass, finite truncation
  error bounds, and an explicit rational Markov-chain representation.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - Syracuse dynamics
  - valuation words
  - terminal residues
  - collision energy
  - second moment
  - Markov chain
repository-code: "https://github.com/s4ztz4bnf6-maker/Lubuimi"
